#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129538 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129285 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "eba1f811-7b7d-56f6-8b49-4e7a4c7db81b" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Moments of Inertia Using Polar Coordinates"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3056ba5d-f7d1-55a3-8c91-5da94f695f90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426091} {:answer/id #uuid "32392a3b-31a7-5a44-8746-b4c85858d143" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426092} {:answer/id #uuid "77d105e7-3ddf-576d-b7fd-6524428a349e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4-2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426108} {:answer/id #uuid "7faf887c-1e04-5044-ade7-d44593ea0768" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8-3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426111} {:answer/id #uuid "d52f3d90-a693-584a-a56c-1a94156d2638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426136}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d52f3d90-a693-584a-a56c-1a94156d2638" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10-4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426136} :answer-field/id #uuid "1239f0fe-7d29-5b4f-895a-1d599c74b28e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126725}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "41c034f9-14b4-5bc4-9351-1214f69c2032" :question/math-academy-id "q-162990" :question/problem "![](images/0a/0a85b0be5f8e5db2cf4d1716e4afe4a2780c500d94a1ce282a9d0044f93ba084.png)\n\nConsider the plate that occupies the region $D$ enclosed by the polar circles $r=1$ and $r=\\sqrt{3}$ and the polar rays $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ and $\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ in the first quadrant, as shown above. The mass density function of the plate is given by $\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{6}{x}.$ Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (r,\\theta ),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin, in polar coordinates, is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta ={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nFirst, note that the region $D$ in polar coordinates can be expressed as\n\n$$\nD=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le \\sqrt{3},\\,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi }{3}\\}.\n$$\n\nAlso, the mass density function in polar coordinates is \n\n$$\n\\lambda (r,\\theta )=\\frac{6}{r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta }=\\frac{6}{r}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta .\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}\\lambda (r,\\theta )\\cdot {r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}(\\frac{6}{r}\\operatorname{sec}⁡\\theta ){r}^{3}{cos}^{2}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}{\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}6{r}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =({\\int }_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}6{r}^{2}\\,\\text{d}r)({\\int }_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta \\,\\text{d}\\theta ) \\\\  & =2{r}^{3}{|}_{1}^{\\sqrt{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta {|}_{\\pi /6}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =2(3\\sqrt{3}-1)\\cdot (\\frac{\\sqrt{3}-1}{2}) \\\\  & =(3\\sqrt{3}-1)\\cdot (\\sqrt{3}-1) \\\\  & =10-4\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fdc1a2a-8a35-59f2-9890-5b835693df4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "080d8399-ca6e-5bfc-9948-10e6f55ec587" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3.4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426079} {:answer/id #uuid "52708feb-3913-5690-b2e1-2173e86cf70b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426102} {:answer/id #uuid "591fa420-a919-5ad2-a1d5-c2c1c7db9500" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.8\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426103} {:answer/id #uuid "9c33f085-6253-5add-a526-e7a9b5dd2021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426126} {:answer/id #uuid "a184fae6-ae92-58da-b4e6-91168995a1c8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426128}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9c33f085-6253-5add-a526-e7a9b5dd2021" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426126} :answer-field/id #uuid "6289bd5c-72da-5cc5-87b8-932a6822cc65" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426152}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "d5a11202-6be7-5636-bb7a-f06e82bc2539" :question/math-academy-id "q-163145" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,2\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 1\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2}^{4}{y}^{2}\\cdot x{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[{\\int }_{2}^{4}x{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{4}{[\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}]}_{2}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{y}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[\\frac{6}{5}{y}^{5}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{5}-0 \\\\  & =1.2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $x$-axis is $1.2\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186281611 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129212 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3fdc1a2a-8a35-59f2-9890-5b835693df4f" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina Given a Mass Density Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00586df5-9953-5e7a-a58f-2329aa16a468" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278586} {:answer/id #uuid "3bf84ed5-f917-50b8-8e4d-80368c472356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279121} {:answer/id #uuid "4237198b-add2-521b-b160-d585a0924755" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279184} {:answer/id #uuid "58055d99-9594-5371-bd9f-20b8d761809d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279400} {:answer/id #uuid "86941ae5-17f0-581b-91b1-2673bcdf9949" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279793}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3bf84ed5-f917-50b8-8e4d-80368c472356" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186279121} :answer-field/id #uuid "945c0f7a-70d5-5057-8a4c-71bc5f6f818a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281099}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e73bf43d-4842-564c-b994-8b4ed88b9ee2" :question/math-academy-id "q-163146" :question/problem "A rectangular plate occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\}$\nwith mass density function $\\lambda (x,y)=(x+y)\\,\\text{kg}/{\\text{m}}^{2},$ where $x$ and $y$ area measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of this lamina about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{2}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}[{\\int }_{0}^{2}{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}y\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}y]}_{x=0}^{x=2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{3}4+\\frac{8y}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[4y+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{3}]}_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =12+12 \\\\  & =24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia of the lamina about the $y$-axis is $24\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426169 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "21e7bd91-295b-518a-b561-81121cd85323" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426086} {:answer/id #uuid "3b931fa2-83ac-51fe-bb7c-19a20e4185e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426095} {:answer/id #uuid "3ff58e4c-ec26-5573-9e2f-2d04c31bdf0d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426098} {:answer/id #uuid "4723d509-fb10-5fce-b47c-17128e37c80a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426100} {:answer/id #uuid "68bfb188-a994-53ac-b526-94cd37c66536" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426104}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3b931fa2-83ac-51fe-bb7c-19a20e4185e2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{7M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426095} :answer-field/id #uuid "d64a47db-1f98-5942-95f8-0a5fe8a1d806" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426159}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a576d72d-3059-5635-bf8f-38bb7570610e" :question/math-academy-id "q-163202" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 2,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $y$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=1\\cdot 3=3.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{3}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{y},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{y} & ={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{2}{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}{[\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{1}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{3}{\\int }_{0}^{3}\\frac{7}{3}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{9}[y]_{0}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{7M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{7M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186426168 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129211 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "92cc3d27-0e31-571f-9b92-4f209c5a08e0" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Moment of Inertia of a Lamina With Uniform Mass Density"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1a308805-aad8-54a7-b5b1-064462e81b88" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{22M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426082} {:answer/id #uuid "383fad8b-59a8-5b43-ad3d-50f07ba39230" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426094} {:answer/id #uuid "7cd77a93-c9ac-5031-8c15-eb3b4d405d24" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26M\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426110} {:answer/id #uuid "b11137df-53c8-5030-b8e0-6a9bb71fdcb0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{16M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426131} {:answer/id #uuid "f370ad7c-77cf-51a3-8d2a-a9e647d5cb34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426145}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f370ad7c-77cf-51a3-8d2a-a9e647d5cb34" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{13M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426145} :answer-field/id #uuid "73ed7367-47d9-5ab5-97c8-cd0c7ced1597" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186426153}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a005e400-255d-52bf-b2df-866a68951503" :question/math-academy-id "q-163203" :question/problem "A rectangular plate of mass $M\\,\\text{kg}$ and uniform mass density occupies the region\n$D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 4,\\,\\,1\\le y\\le 3\\},$ where $x$ and $y$ are measured in meters. Find the moment of inertia of the plate about the $x$-axis." :question/worked-solution "For a plane lamina $D$ with mass density function $\\lambda (x,y),$ we have the following definitions:\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $x$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{x}={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the $y$-axis is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{y}={∬}_{D}{x}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\n- The moment of inertia about the origin is given by\n\n$$\n{I}_{0}={∬}_{D}({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A={I}_{x}+{I}_{y}.\n$$\n\nThe area of the rectangular plate $D$ is $A=3\\cdot 2=6.$ \n\nSince the plate has uniform density, every unit of area contains the same amount of mass. Therefore, the mass density is constant and is given by the total mass divided by the total area:\n\n$$\n\\lambda (x,y)=\\frac{M}{A}=\\frac{M}{6}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for ${I}_{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{I}_{x} & ={∬}_{D}{y}^{2}\\lambda (x,y)\\,\\text{d}A \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{\\int }_{1}^{4}{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}{y}^{2}[x]_{1}^{4}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{\\int }_{1}^{3}3{y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}{[{y}^{3}]}_{1}^{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{M}{6}(27-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{13M}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the moment of inertia is $\\frac{13M}{3}\\,\\text{kg}\\cdot {\\text{m}}^{2}.$"}]}
